"CD-160 APPLICATION AND NOTICE OF APPLICATION AND HEARING FOR ORDER TO QUASH EX PARTE WRIT OF POSSESSION (Claim and Delivery) (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/cd160.pdf)\nciteturn1679search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.9 years ago; Crawled: 4.4 years ago; CD-160 ... SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF\nCD-160\n\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name, State Bar number, and address):\n\nTELEPHONE NO.:  \nFAX NO. (Optional):  \nE-MAIL ADDRESS (Optional):  \nATTORNEY FOR (Name):\n\nSUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF  \nSTREET ADDRESS:  \nMAILING ADDRESS:  \nCITY AND ZIP CODE:  \nBRANCH NAME:\n\nPLAINTIFF:  \nDEFENDANT:\n\nFOR COURT USE ONLY\n\nCASE NUMBER:\n\nAPPLICATION AND NOTICE OF APPLICATION AND HEARING FOR ORDER TO QUASH EX PARTE WRIT OF POSSESSION\n\nTO PLAINTIFF* (name):\n\n1. You are notified that defendant (name): applies for (check all that apply):\n\n   a. ☐ An order to quash the ex parte writ of possession issued on (date): and an order releasing any levied property.  \n   b. ☐ Damages sustained by the defendant proximately caused by the levy of the writ of possession and the loss of possession of the property caused by the levy under Code of Civil Procedure section 512.020(b)(3)(iii).  \n   c. ☐ An order staying delivery of the property pending the court hearing.\n\n2. A hearing will be held in this court, as follows:\n\n   a. Date: ________   Time: ________   ☐ Dept.: ________   ☐ Rm.: ________  \n   b. Address of court: ☐ same as noted above   ☐ is (specify):\n\n3. ☐ This application is made on the ground that the plaintiff is not entitled to a writ of possession. This application is supported by the ☐ verified answer ☐ attached declaration or declarations and attached memorandum of points and authorities.\n\n4. Number of pages attached: ________\n\nDated:\n\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME OF DEFENDANT OR ATTORNEY)  \n(SIGNATURE OF DEFENDANT OR ATTORNEY)\n\n* “Plaintiff” includes cross-complainant, and “defendant” includes cross-defendant.\n\nPage 1 of 1\n\nForm Adopted for Mandatory Use  \nJudicial Council of California  \nCD-160 [Rev. January 1, 2006]\n\nAPPLICATION AND NOTICE OF APPLICATION AND HEARING FOR ORDER TO QUASH EX PARTE WRIT OF POSSESSION  \n(Claim and Delivery)\n\nCode Civ. Proc., §§ 512.020, 512.050--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApplication and Notice of Application and Hearing for Order to Quash Ex Parte Writ of Possession | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/CD-160)\nciteturn1679search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Application and Notice of Application and Hearing for Order to Quash Ex Parte Writ of Possession (CD-160)Ask the court to cancel (quash) a writ of possession  (an order telling the sheriff to take and hold property that that you have that the plaintiff  claims is theirs) that the court made without holding a hearing (ex parte).\n\n# Application and Notice of Application and Hearing for Order to Quash Ex Parte Writ of Possession (CD-160)\n\nAsk the court to cancel (quash) a writ of possession  (an order telling the sheriff to take and hold property that that you have that the plaintiff  claims is theirs) that the court made without holding a hearing (ex parte). Can also be used to ask the court to place a hold on (stay) taking the property or to order the plaintiff to pay you for what you lost when the sheriff took the property from you. Also tells the plaintiff when the court will hold a hearing on your request.\n\nGet form CD-160\n\nEffective: January 1, 2006--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neFiling Finder (https://riverside.courts.ca.gov/mServices/eFilingFinder/efiling-finder.php)\nciteturn1679search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Limited/Unlimited Civil  | Hearing Documents  | Application and Notice of Application and Hearing for Order to Quash Ex Parte Writ of Possession - Claim and Delivery (CD-1